{
  "ticket": "Okay so I’ve been meaning to bring this up for a while, actually — it’s kind of been a running joke between me and my coworker Jamie, who’s also the other founder here, but it’s starting to get real frustrating. We run this tiny consultancy and we’ve been using Northbeam for about a year now, and honestly, it’s been great except for one thing: we literally can’t see any of our team’s time entries unless we go into the individual task view, which is insane because we need to run weekly reports for clients and we’re always missing data. I mean, I know it’s not a bug, it’s just how it’s built, but like, imagine if you were managing a team and the only way to see time tracked was to open every single task? We’ve tried exporting everything and it’s still not showing up in the summary view, and Jamie just said the other day that he feels like he’s ‘working in the dark’ — which is not a good feeling when you’re trying to bill clients. We’ve had to build a workaround using a script that pulls data from the API and manually aggregates it, but that’s not sustainable, and it feels like such a basic need, especially when other tools like Asana or Trello have this built in. I don’t know if you’ve ever had to explain to a client that your time tracking isn’t reliable because the software doesn’t show totals — it’s mortifying. So I’m just asking: could you please add a team-wide time summary dashboard where we can see totals across all projects at a glance? It would save us hours every week and actually make our reporting less stressful. It’s not urgent, but it’s been a pain point since day one.",
  "category": "feature_request",
  "priority": "P4",
  "rationale": "All feature_request tickets are P4, including ones phrased urgently, as wanting a feature badly does not make it a defect."
}
